{"name":"Gnome","hex":"#81a19b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gnome","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elemental (spirit or corporeal creature associated with a classical element) associated with earth.","One of a race of imaginary human-like beings, usually depicted as short and typically bearded males, who inhabit the inner parts of the earth and act as guardians of mines, mineral treasure, etc.; in modern fantasy literature and games, when distinguished from dwarves, gnomes are usually smaller than dwarves and more focused on engineering than mining."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A brief reflection or maxim; a pithy saying."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gnome"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gnome","blocks":[{"text":"A gnome is a mythological creature and diminutive spirit in Renaissance magic and alchemy, introduced by the Swiss physician and alchemist Paracelsus in the 16th century, and widely adopted by authors, including those of modern fantasy literature. They are typically depicted as small humanoids who live underground. Gnome characteristics are reinterpreted to suit various storytellers and artists."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Heinrich_Schlitt_Gnom_mit_Zeitung_und_Tabakspfeife.jpg/330px-Heinrich_Schlitt_Gnom_mit_Zeitung_und_Tabakspfeife.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gnome","wikidata":"Q188215"},{"title":"GNOME","blocks":[{"text":"GNOME is a desktop environment and suite of software for Linux and BSD developed by the GNOME Project and released as free and open source software. The primary components of GNOME are the GNOME Shell, which provides features such as virtual desktops and window management; and the GNOME Core Applications, which distribute a suite of software that integrates with the shell and provides basic system features such as a file manager and a computer configuration application."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Gnomelogo.svg/330px-Gnomelogo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNOME","wikidata":"Q44316"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Olaus%281555%29-Hist_septentrionalibus-p210-demons-in-mines.jpg/500px-Olaus%281555%29-Hist_septentrionalibus-p210-demons-in-mines.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Olaus%281555%29-Hist_septentrionalibus-p210-demons-in-mines.jpg/500px-Olaus%281555%29-Hist_septentrionalibus-p210-demons-in-mines.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Demons in the mine. Olaus Magnus, Historia de gentibus septentrionalibus[87][77]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOlaus(1555)-Hist_septentrionalibus-p210-demons-in-mines.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Praetorius%281668%29-p0000-02Bergm%C3%A4nnerlein_Wichtelin_Unter-Irrdische.jpg/330px-Praetorius%281668%29-p0000-02Bergm%C3%A4nnerlein_Wichtelin_Unter-Irrdische.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Praetorius%281668%29-p0000-02Bergm%C3%A4nnerlein_Wichtelin_Unter-Irrdische.jpg/330px-Praetorius%281668%29-p0000-02Bergm%C3%A4nnerlein_Wichtelin_Unter-Irrdische.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bergmännerlein, Wights, and Subterraneans (Unter-Irrdische). Engraving by Thomas Cross, Sr. (fl. 1632–1682), frontispiece to Praetorius (1668) [1666] Anthropodemus Plutonicus.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APraetorius(1668)-p0000-02Bergm%C3%A4nnerlein_Wichtelin_Unter-Irrdische.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Lichttaler_